In the rectangular coordinate system xOy, the parametric equations of the curve C₁ are $$\begin{cases} x=cost \\ y=sin^{2}t \end{cases}$$ (where t is the parameter). Establish a polar coordinate system with the coordinate origin as the pole and the positive semi-axis of the x-axis as the polar axis. The polar coordinate equation of the line C₂ is $$ρ(sinθ-acosθ)= \frac {1}{2}$$ (a∈R).
(1) Write the ordinary equation of the curve C₁ and the rectangular coordinate equation of the line C₂;
(2) If the line C₂ intersects with the curve C₁ at two distinct points, find the range of values for a.

Given that $\tan \alpha=3$, find:

(1) The value of $\frac{\sin \alpha + \cos \alpha}{\sin \alpha - \cos \alpha}$;

(2) The value of $\cos \alpha - \sin \alpha$ if $\pi < \alpha < \frac{3\pi}{2}$.

Given the functions $f(x)=\sin x-ax$ and $g(x)=bx\cos x\ (a\in R,b\in R)$.
(1) Discuss the monotonicity of the function $f(x)$ in the interval $(0,\pi)$;
(2) If $a=2b$ and $a\geqslant \frac {2}{3}$, prove that $f(x) < g(x)$ when $x > 0$.

