(Ⅰ) If $|AB|=\sqrt{15}$, find the equation of line $l$;  
(Ⅱ) Is there a fixed point $M(x_0, 0)$ on the x-axis, such that the sum of the slopes of lines $MA$ and $MB$ is always zero as $l$ varies? If it exists, find the value of $x_0$; if not, explain why.

In the Cartesian coordinate system $xOy$, the vertex of the parabola $C$ is the center of the hyperbola $D$: $$\frac{y^2}{2} - x^2 = \frac{1}{3}.$$ The focus of the parabola $C$ coincides with the foci of the hyperbola $D$.

(1) Find the equation of the parabola $C$;
(2) If the point $P(t, 1)$ ($t > 0$) is a fixed point on the parabola $C$, and $A$, $B$ are two moving points on the parabola $C$ such that $PA \perp PB$, determine whether the line $AB$ passes through a fixed point. If it does, find the fixed point; if not, explain why.

