(1) Find the equation of the ellipse $C$;  
(2) On the line $x=2 \sqrt {3}$, there are two points $M$ and $N$ ($M$ is in the first quadrant) such that $\overrightarrow {F_{1}M} \cdot \overrightarrow {F_{2}N}=0$, and the line $MF_1$ intersects with $NF_2$ at point $Q$. When $|MN|$ is minimized, find the length of the segment $MQ$.

