In acute triangle $\triangle ABC$, the sides opposite to angles $A$, $B$, and $C$ are $a$, $b$, and $c$, respectively. Given that $\sin A= \frac{3 \sqrt{10}}{10}$ and $a\sin A+b\sin B=c\sin C+ \frac{2 \sqrt{5}}{5}a\sin B$.

