Given the coordinates of points A, B, and C are A(-2, -2), B(-2, 6), and C(4, -2) respectively, and express point P as (a, b). We can calculate the square of the distances from P to A, B, and C as follows:
\begin{align*}
|PA|^{2} &= (a + 2)^{2} + (b + 2)^{2}, \\
|PB|^{2} &= (a + 2)^{2} + (b - 6)^{2}, \\
|PC|^{2} &= (a - 4)^{2} + (b + 2)^{2}.
\end{align*}

Summing up these distances, we get:
\begin{align*}
|PA|^{2}+|PB|^{2}+|PC|^{2} &= (a + 2)^{2} + (b + 2)^{2} + (a + 2)^{2} + (b - 6)^{2} + (a - 4)^{2} + (b + 2)^{2} \\
&= 3a^{2} + 3b^{2} - 4b + 68.
\end{align*}

Since point P is on the circle $x^{2}+y^{2}=4$, we have that $a^{2}+b^{2}=4$. We can express $a^{2}$ as $a^{2}=4-b^{2}$, which must be non-negative, hence $b^{2} \leq 4$.

Thus, the possible range for $b$ is $-2 \leq b \leq 2$. Substituting $a^{2}=4-b^{2}$ into the sum expression, we obtain:
\begin{align*}
|PA|^{2}+|PB|^{2}+|PC|^{2} &= 12 - 3b^{2} + 3b^{2} - 4b + 68 \\
&= -4b + 80.
\end{align*}

As $b$ ranges from -2 to 2, the value of $-4b$ will range between -8 and 8. Consequently, $-4b + 80$ will range between 72 and 88.

Therefore, the maximum value is 88 and the minimum value is 72, and the sum of the maximum and minimum values is $\boxed{88 + 72 = 160}$.

